# A deployment's own make settings for controller/ (docs/rollout.md, This site). Copy this to
# controller/local.mk in the main checkout (untracked: .gitignore; every git worktree reads
# the main checkout's) and put your own values in. The project's Makefile has no default for
# any of them: without one, a target that needs it stops and names it. Use ?= so the command
# line and the environment still win (make fleet-rollout-dry NODES=... for once).
# Documentation addresses (RFC 5737) below: put your own.

# ---- The fleet ----
# The nodes a rollout changes, in rollout order after the canary (KIND=firmware, blocklist,
# overrides, zones). Usually the same as settings.json's "nodes".
NODES              ?= 192.0.2.52 192.0.2.53
# Changed first, if it is one of the nodes changed; empty: settings.json's "canary" (the Push
# page's too) if it is one of them, else the first of them
CANARY             ?= 192.0.2.52
# The catalog boards (boards/<board>.json) whose transitional firmware the nodes run: make
# fleet-firmware builds them (with firmware/local.mk's STATIC_IP_<board>), KIND=firmware
# pushes them. No two may share a chip image.
FLEET_BOARDS       ?= p4-ip101 ws-s3-eth
# KIND=config's usual node and its config (in the data directory's configs/), host=file
CONFIGS            ?= 192.0.2.53=node1.json

# ---- Secrets ----
# Secrets are never written here: each comes from an environment variable (export it, or let
# SECRET_RUN put it there) or a file. The zone primary's API token (a primary of a kind with
# an API, e.g. technitium): the environment variable that holds it. None: adoption uses the
# token make primary-import put in the data directory, if any.
#PRIMARY_TOKEN_ENV    ?= ESPDNS_PRIMARY_TOKEN
# The release signing key: $ESPDNS_RELEASE_KEY (the PEM, or base64 of it), or a file
#RELEASE_KEY_FILE     ?= ../firmware/secrets/release.pem
# A password manager's command that runs a command with the named variables set to their
# secrets: $(1) is the list of variable names (ESPDNS_RELEASE_KEY, PRIMARY_TOKEN_ENV's,
# ESPDNS_ADMIN_PASSWORD, ESPDNS_BACKUP_PASSPHRASE). Use = (not :=), so $(1) is filled in.
#SECRET_RUN            = /path/to/secrets-tool exec $(1) --

# ---- The data directory ----
# Seed a new data directory from your own files, kept outside the repo (make data copies
# them only where there is no file yet): a settings.json, and a directory of node configs.
#SETTINGS_SEED      ?= /path/to/settings.json
#CONFIG_SEEDS       ?= /path/to/configs
